## Engineering handbook
Handbook version: see `HANDBOOK_VERSION`. Standards are vendored in `docs/engineering-handbook/`.
Read them before starting work. The project-specific rules above and any exceptions below take
precedence over the handbook.

Non-negotiable:
- Push and open PRs only to `{{OWNER/REPO}}`, always with
  `gh pr create --repo {{OWNER/REPO}} --base {{BRANCH}} --head <branch>`. Verify the destination
  first. Never push to or open a PR against the parent repository without the human owner's explicit
  authorisation for that contribution. Treat upstream remotes as read-only.
- Never commit to `{{BRANCH}}`. Never force-push. Never merge or deploy; the human owner does that.
- Never commit, print or paste secrets.
- Report results honestly: implemented, tested, reviewed, merged and deployed are different things.

